 To configure this, set `stake_amount="unlimited"`. We also recommend to set `tradable_balance_ratio=0.99` (99%) - to keep a minimum balance for eventual fees.
 
+#### Exposure per underlying currency
+
+If you trade several pairs that are all priced against, or settled in, the same underlying currency (for example a handful of BTC-margined futures, or several coins that are all quoted in the same stablecoin), a string of otherwise-independent winning-looking trades can still leave you with an outsized exposure to that one currency - if it moves against you, all of those positions get hit at once.
+
+`max_single_currency_exposure` limits this: it caps the combined stake amount of all *currently open* trades sharing a pair's quote/settlement currency to at most this share of total tradable capital, regardless of how the individual trades were sized.
+
+```json
+"max_single_currency_exposure": 0.5,
+```
+
+With the above, no more than 50% of tradable capital may ever be committed at once to trades quoted in the same underlying currency. When opening (or adding to, via [position adjustment](strategy-callbacks.md#adjust-trade-position)) a trade would push that combined exposure over the limit, the stake amount for that trade is reduced to fit under the limit - or the trade is skipped entirely if no stake would remain. This is reported the same way other stake-sizing adjustments (e.g. balance-constrained resizing) already are: logged in live/dry-run, and applied silently in backtesting since backtesting doesn't log per-candle sizing decisions either.
+
+This setting can also be set (or overridden) at the strategy level - see [Strategy Override](#parameters-in-the-strategy).
+
+!!! Note
+    This limit is evaluated in the same shared sizing logic used by both live/dry-run and backtesting, so it applies identically in both modes.
+
+!!! Note
+    Leave this setting unset to disable the check (the default).
+
